.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt MORE 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm more
.Nd page text to a terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n Ar lines
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility writes
.Ar file
contents to standard output, pausing after each page when the output is a
terminal. Space advances one page, Enter advances one line and
.Ql q
quits. A non-terminal output streams everything without paging.
.Fl n
sets the page height (default 24).
.Pp
The target image has no generic standard-input stream; file operands are required.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cat 1 ,
.Xr write 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the documented POSIX more subset.
